# Next.js Web Control Plane Conventions

- Use Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict mode, Tailwind CSS, and shadcn/ui primitives (`src/components/ui/`).
- Group routes cleanly under `src/app/(auth)/`, `src/app/(onboarding)/`, and `src/app/(dashboard)/` (`brain`, `connectors`, `jobs`, `approvals`, `runs`, `policies`, `billing`, `settings`).
- Consume backend endpoints exclusively via the generated OpenAPI client in `src/lib/api-client/` — do not hand-write untyped `fetch` calls or duplicate backend Pydantic schemas.
- Default to Server Components for data fetching and keep Client Components small and focused on interactive controls (memory editing, approval actions, policy editors, artifact previews).
- Never render unverified citations or raw artifact bucket paths; display source links + timestamps and use backend-issued signed URLs for downloads.
